han Leonora(50)? Midpoint 50/52 is 51. If secret 51, tie. If secret 50, Leonora wins. If secret 46, Leonora dist 4, Daniel dist 6. Leonora wins. So Daniel is not always the threat on the low end. But my range starts at 46. If secret is 46, Leonora(50) is dist 4. Daniel(52) is dist 6. I(66) is dist 20. Leonora wins. If I guessed 52, I'd be dist 6. Still Leonora wins. If I guessed 50, I'd tie Leonora. But 50 is far from my midpoint 66. The secret is uniform in 46-85. I should guess the number that maximizes my expected score. Guessing the midpoint of my range (66) is generally optimal against random opponents, but here opponents are strategic. Eileen is at 75, Daniel at 52. The 'safe' zone for me is between them. 66 is the midpoint of 52 and 75? (52+75)/2 = 63.5. So if I guess 64, I am exactly equidistant. If I guess 64: vs 52, I win if secret > 58. vs 75, I win if secret < 65. So I win 59-64. That's 6 numbers. 6/40 = 15% chance of 3 points. EV 0.45. This is worse than guessing 66 (11 numbers, 27.5%). Why? Because my range is 46-85. The center is 66. Guessing the center of my own vision is usually best. Let's stick with 66. It covers the most likely area where I am the closest or tied.",
